        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "356d4677-9b1b-53c1-84a9-68ac99274cef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: TT31\n- People: Khonsu, Thutmose III\n- Roles: First Prophet of Menkheperre, Pharaoh\n- Topics: Ancient Egypt, Eighteenth Dynasty, 19th Dynasty, 20th Dynasty\n\nFacts:\n- Thutmose III was the sixth Pharaoh of the Eighteenth Dynasty.\n- Thutmose III was sometimes read as Thutmosis or Tuthmosis III, called Thothmes in older historical works, and his name means \"Thoth is born.\"\n- TT31 is the burial place of the Ancient Egyptian official Khonsu.\n- Khonsu served as First Prophet of Menkheperre, who was Thutmose III.\n- Khonsu held that role during either the 19th Dynasty or the 20th Dynasty.",
